+# Changes, round 2
+
+Only src/statement.mjs changed. captures/ regenerated with `npm run capture`. `npm test` passes.
+
+## Gaps closed (largest first)
+1. Ordering: charges now sort by amount, largest first, ties by service name (Key management before Load balancing). Credits sort largest first (Committed-use discount 410.63, then Service credit 164.25).
+2. Zero-usage services: Machine learning inference and Monitoring are no longer table rows. A wrapped sentence after the total-due block gives the count and names them.
+3. Share column: added left of Amount, one decimal, decimal points aligned (39.5, 31.2, 12.0, 9.5, 5.0, 1.0, 0.9, 0.9), computed in integer arithmetic; the charges subtotal shows 100.0%. Credits and total due have no share.
+4. Credits and currency: credits are written in parentheses, e.g. (410.63), with the closing parenthesis one column right of the amounts so digits stay aligned. Currency is named once, in the "Amount (USD)" heading; the last line is "Total due".
+5. Header: line 1 is "Northwind Robotics" with "Account NW-20418" right-aligned to the table edge; line 2 is "Usage statement for September 2026".
+
+Totals unchanged and exact: 4,155.66 - 410.63 - 164.25 = 3,580.78. Widest line 64 characters, no tabs, no trailing spaces, ASCII only.
+
+## Left on purpose
+- "Total charges" label kept (critic did not count it as a gap).
+- "=" rules around the total due kept (not counted as a gap).
+- No "$" signs on amounts; the column heading carries the currency.
+- No payment terms, due date or footer beyond the unlisted-services sentence: the data supplies none.
+- Tests unchanged: they only check that customer, account, services and credits are named, which still holds (the zero-usage services are named in the foot sentence).
